<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Cloud & DevOps Engineer Resume</title>
    <style>
        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;
            color: #222;
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
            line-height: 1.4;
            font-size: 13px;
        }
        .page {
            width: 8.5in;
            height: 11in;
            background: #fff;
            margin: 20px auto;
            padding: 0.4in 0.5in;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        header {
            border-bottom: 2px solid #0056b3;
            padding-bottom: 8px;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
        }
        h1 {
            font-size: 22px;
            color: #0056b3;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.5px;
        }
        .subtitle {
            font-size: 14px;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #444;
            margin-bottom: 4px;
        }
        .contact {
            font-size: 11px;
            color: #555;
        }
        .contact span {
            margin-right: 12px;
        }
        section {
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }
        h2 {
            font-size: 13px;
            color: #0056b3;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
            padding-bottom: 2px;
            margin-bottom: 6px;
            letter-spacing: 0.5px;
        }
        .skills-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr;
            row-gap: 3px;
            font-size: 12px;
        }
        .skills-category {
            font-weight: bold;
            color: #333;
        }
        .job {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }
        .job-header {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 12.5px;
            color: #222;
        }
        .job-title {
            font-style: italic;
            color: #444;
            font-size: 11.5px;
            margin-bottom: 3px;
        }
        ul {
            list-style-type: square;
            padding-left: 16px;
        }
        li {
            margin-bottom: 2px;
            font-size: 11.5px;
            color: #333;
        }
        .education-item {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            font-size: 12px;
        }
        @media print {
            body {
                background: none;
            }
            .page {
                margin: 0;
                box-shadow: none;
                width: 100%;
                height: 100%;
                padding: 0.3in 0.4in;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
    <header>
        <h1>John Williams</h1>
        <div class="subtitle">Senior Cloud & DevOps Engineer</div>
        <div class="contact">
            <span><strong>Phone:</strong> (555) 019-2831</span>
            <span><strong>Email:</strong> john.williams@example.com</span>
            <span><strong>Location:</strong> Houston, TX</span>
            <span><strong>LinkedIn:</strong> linkedin.com/in/example</span>
            <span><strong>GitHub:</strong> github.com/example</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2>Professional Summary</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 11.5px; color: #333;">
            Results-driven Cloud & DevOps Engineer with 6 years of hands-on experience designing, automating, and scaling high-availability enterprise infrastructure across AWS and hybrid Linux environments. Specialized in Infrastructure as Code (Terraform), CI/CD pipeline automation (Jenkins, GitHub Actions), container orchestration (Docker, ECS, Kubernetes), and security configuration management (Ansible). Proven track record of reducing deployment overhead and optimizing cloud architectures.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Technical Core Competencies</h2>
        <div class="skills-grid">
            <div class="skills-category">Cloud Platforms:</div>
            <div>AWS (EC2, VPC, S3, ECS, Fargate, ALB, IAM, CloudFront, ACM, CloudWatch)</div>
            
            <div class="skills-category">IaC & Automation:</div>
            <div>Terraform, Ansible, RHEL System Roles, CloudFormation, Jinja2</div>
            
            <div class="skills-category">Containers & CI/CD:</div>
            <div>Docker, Kubernetes, OpenShift, Jenkins, GitHub Actions, Git</div>
            
            <div class="skills-category">Linux & Scripting:</div>
            <div>RHEL/CentOS, Debian, Bash Scripting, Python, Systemd, LVM, Network/Firewalld</div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Professional Experience</h2>

        <div class="job">
            <div class="job-header">
                <span>National Oilwell Varco</span>
                <span>2024 – Present</span>
            </div>
            <div class="job-title">Infrastructure Automation Engineer</div>
            <ul>
                <li>Architected reusable Terraform modules to automate AWS VPC, EC2, and ECS Fargate deployments, reducing provisioning cycles by 60%.</li>
                <li>Built automated CI/CD pipelines using Jenkins and GitHub Actions with AWS OIDC authentication, accelerating deployment speed.</li>
                <li>Developed modular Ansible playbooks to manage production user access, SSH key distribution, and security hardening across 100+ Linux instances.</li>
                <li>Configured Application Load Balancers (ALB) and target-tracking auto-scaling policies to maintain 99.99% service availability during traffic spikes.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="job">
            <div class="job-header">
                <span>CenterPoint Energy</span>
                <span>2020 – 2024</span>
            </div>
            <div class="job-title">Systems & GIS Engineer</div>
            <ul>
                <li>Administered enterprise Linux environments (RHEL), managing LVM storage, firewalld policies, system roles, and patch management.</li>
                <li>Integrated Ansible with Terraform using local-exec provisions to automatically configure newly created AWS instances post-provisioning.</li>
                <li>Optimized cloud storage infrastructure on AWS S3 and automated dynamic DNS records and certificate management via ACM.</li>
                <li>Collaborated with cybersecurity teams to perform vulnerability remediation, SIEM root-cause analysis, and system hardening.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="job">
            <div class="job-header">
                <span>DR Financial Services / iCare Medical</span>
                <span>2018 – 2020</span>
            </div>
            <div class="job-title">Systems Administrator</div>
            <ul>
                <li>Managed virtualized infrastructure on VMware ESXi and vSphere alongside core Linux/Unix servers.</li>
                <li>Automated daily system maintenance, backup verification, and log rotation tasks using custom Bash and Python scripts.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Certifications & Education</h2>
        <div class="education-item">
            <span><strong>Red Hat Certified Engineer (RHCE - EX294)</strong> – Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9</span>
            <span>In Progress / Target 2026</span>
        </div>
        <div class="education-item" style="margin-top: 2px;">
            <span><strong>Bachelor of Science in Information Technology</strong></span>
            <span>Graduated 2018</span>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

</body>
</html>